**Feedback RPC loop — `src/lib/feedback.functions.ts:49-51`** (still present)
```ts
for (const memoryId of new Set(rows.map((r) => r.memory_id))) {
  await supabase.rpc("bump_memory_importance", { p_memory_id: memoryId, p_delta: delta });
}
```
Up to 6 sequential round trips per user rating (RF-02 recalls k=6 memories). Fix: one array-typed RPC —
```sql
create function bump_memory_importance_batch(p_memory_ids uuid[], p_delta int)
returns void as $$
  update agent_memory set importance = least(5, greatest(1, importance + p_delta))
  where id = any(p_memory_ids);
$$ language sql;
```

**Same shape in `src/lib/decision-judgment.functions.ts:260-262`** — `bump_decision_cited_by` looped per cited decision on every judgment write. Same batched-RPC fix applies.

**BYOK-key / account resolution — `src/lib/ai/runtime.server.ts`** — not a row-loop, but `resolveCreditAccountId` (hits `workspaces` + the `ensure_user_default_account` RPC) is independently re-resolved from three call sites per single `callModel`/`callModelStream` invocation: `assertAccountCredits` (:974), `resolveCallKey`→`byokAllowedForCall` (:422, re-invoked per retry at :1447/:1923), and `debitAccountCredits` (:1109). With `maxRetries=2` that's 4-5 round trips resolving the identical `(userId, workspaceId)` — and the 6-step agent loop (`loop.server.ts:839`) repeats this every step, ~20-30 redundant round trips per chat turn.
```ts
const accountIdCache = new Map<string, Promise<string | null>>();
function resolveCreditAccountIdCached(supabase, userId, workspaceId) {
  const key = `${userId}:${workspaceId ?? ""}`;
  if (!accountIdCache.has(key)) accountIdCache.set(key, resolveCreditAccountId(supabase, userId, workspaceId));
  return accountIdCache.get(key)!;
}
```
`creditsEnabled` already has a TTL cache at `runtime.server.ts:860` — this just extends that pattern.

**`BetCard`/`RoadmapColumns` — `src/components/plan/RoadmapColumns.tsx:307-313`** — the `itemsByBucket` grouping genuinely is `useMemo`'d correctly now (keyed on `items`, not `selectedIds`). But `BetCard` (`memo`-wrapped at `BetCard.tsx:322`) still gets fresh callback identities every render:
```tsx
onToggleSelect={(on) => toggleSelect(item.id, on)}
onMoveTo={(bucket) => handleMove(item, bucket)}
```
Toggling one card's checkbox re-renders the whole column tree and defeats `memo` for every `BetCard` on the board. Fix: hoist to stable `useCallback`s that take the id as an argument instead of closing over it:
```tsx
const handleToggleSelect = useCallback((id: string, on: boolean) => toggleSelect(id, on), []);
```

**`CalendarPanel.tsx:330-362`** — `allItems` map/spread, a 14-day filter+sort re-parsing `new Date()` per comparison, and a `buckets` reduce all run unmemoized in the render body. The component also owns ~10 `useState` text fields, so typing one character in an event-edit input re-runs the entire date pipeline over the full list. Wrap in `useMemo` keyed on `allItems`.

**`AccountConnectionsSection.tsx:138-220`** — a single `pollRef` is shared across three independent connect mutations (GitHub/native/Suite). Starting a second connect flow before the first's 5-minute window elapses overwrites `pollRef.current`; when the first interval's callback later calls `clearInterval(pollRef.current)`, it clears the *second* interval, orphaning the first — which now runs forever, invalidating queries every 3s for the rest of the session.
```tsx
const startPoll = (key: QueryKey) => {
  if (pollRef.current) clearInterval(pollRef.current);
  const deadline = Date.now() + 5 * 60 * 1000;
  pollRef.current = setInterval(() => {
    qc.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: key });
    if (Date.now() > deadline) { clearInterval(pollRef.current); pollRef.current = undefined; }
  }, 3_000);
};
```

**`CalendarPanel.tsx:211-223`** — worse than the above: `const iv = setInterval(...)` is a bare local, never stored or cleared on unmount. Navigating away from Calendar mid-connect leaves it firing indefinitely.

**`src/lib/connectors/providers/github.server.ts:89`** — `installTokenCache` module-level `Map` has no eviction; low severity but grows unbounded on a long-lived Worker isolate.

**Checked clean:** `GraphCanvasView.tsx` and `FocusDock.tsx` effects have correct cleanup.

